-	  "deferred_reason": "2026-09-07, Palle, answering the Array brief on /spine-brief: 'revive array_tutorial with all nine maps ... Tutorial_Disco yes. Chamber_Arrays no.' The sequence was dissolved into color on 2026-08-24 as its index rung; Array is taken back out of color and the ladder is re-listed in Palle's order, which is dimensional - single, row, 2D, 3D - then pattern, then disco. Chamber_Arrays is the only one not revived: it is a catalyst chamber, not a rung of the ladder. || THE OVERTURE, 2026-09-07 (Palle: 'Array keeps the four rungs as an overture'). Array holds row_3_x, column_3_z, grid_2d_4x4 and grid_3d_4x4x4 although Tutorial_Row, Tutorial_2D_Build and Tutorial_3D now each own one of them. Deliberate: the first hall shows the whole ladder standing at once, and the seven after it take one rung each and make it walkable. Do not 'de-duplicate' this. || THE SUBSETS LEAVE, 2026-09-07 (Palle: 'but these are the artifact on array map so they should not be in the sequence'). Measured: Tutorial_Row holds 3 artifacts and Tutorial_3D holds 6, and EVERY ONE of them already stands in Array. Neither room holds a single thing the overture does not. Once Array is ruled the overture that shows the whole ladder at once, a room that is a strict subset of it is the overture seen twice, not a rung — so both leave the walk. They keep their map files. Tutorial_2D_Build is NOT dropped: it owns gridagent, the only object in the ladder that writes into an array without you. || AND 2D_BUILD TOO, 2026-09-07 (Palle: 'drop Tutorial_2D_Build too, gridagent can move to Array'). Seven of its eight artifacts were already in the overture; the eighth, gridagent — the only object in the ladder that writes into an array without you — moves to Array at (7,4), beside grid_2d_4x4. With that the room is a strict subset like Row and 3D, and leaves for the same reason. || THE UNBRAIDING, 2026-09-07 (Palle). colour was carrying two threads: a COLOUR thread (Nails, Pillar, Walls, Context_Placed) and a PATTERN thread (Pattern_Foundry, Symmetry_Seventeen), diagnosed by the red-thread pass on 2026-09-03 — 'three of the seven rooms contain no colour argument at all'. The pattern rooms leave for a sequence of their own (`tiling`), joined by Tutorial_Pattern and Array_Patterns from array_tutorial. Evidence they are one sequence: pattern_tile_mirror stands in three of the four (Symmetry_Seventeen joins on vr_tile_editor alone), pattern_tile_4x4 in two, pattern_maker_station in two, vr_tile_editor in two. colour's stated truth — 'context, not wavelength' — now applies to every room in colour. || TUTORIAL_SINGLE LEAVES, 2026-09-09 (Palle: 'remove Tutorial_Single from array_tutorial sequence'). It was the ladder's first rung — one cube, one grab — and it goes the way Row, 3D and 2D_Build went: measured, it holds pick_up_cube, dark_sphere and xyz_coordinates against an Array overture that already shows the whole ladder standing at once, and a room whose argument the first hall has already made is the overture seen twice. The walk is now two: Array, then Tutorial_Disco — the ladder shown, then the ladder at scale. The map file stays, its roles ruling and its brief stay, and the book keeps its pearl (one draft line, hero xyz_coordinates) alongside the six others already off the walk. | 2026-09-17: Tutorial_3D explicitly revived with a Menger-style flight enclosure. New monochrome floor and wall studies precede Disco; coloured Disco returns after Color.",
